limitations_reported:
- Prosocial learning was restricted to unknown others, and participants did not meet these others;
- Future research should extend to other beneficiaries (e.g., friends, family);
- The No One condition showed an intermediate neural pattern between Self and Others that is difficult to interpret;
- Model used separate learning rates per condition following Lockwood et al. (2016), but did not compare whether different learning rates/betas are needed across conditions;
- Cross-sectional design — longitudinal studies needed for true developmental trajectories;
- Narrower age range (9–21) may have limited power to detect quadratic age effects

